<main>
  <h1>Ice Age hall</h1>
  <p>The star of this hall is a mammoth skeleton found near Kazan in 1978. The skeleton is 3.2 m tall and about 45,000 years old.</p>
  <figure>
    <img src="/files/mammoth-skeleton.png" alt="Mammoth skeleton">
    <figcaption>The skeleton after cleaning, photographed in 2025.</figcaption>
  </figure>
  <p>Dr. Irina Petrova led the <em>excavation</em>. She still gives a talk here on the first Saturday of each month.</p>
  <img src="/files/placeholder.gif" data-src="/files/woolly-rhino.png" alt="Woolly rhino">
  <img src="/files/mammoth-skeleton.png" alt="Skeleton detail">
  <img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAAAAACw=" alt="">
  <img src="  ../files/cave-lion.png " alt="Cave lion">
  <img data-src="   " src="/files/tusk.jpg" alt="Tusk">
  <p>Related objects: <a href="/exhibits/1">the mammoth tusk</a> and <a href="/exhibits/2">a cave lion skull</a>.</p>
  <noscript>
    <style>.qznoscript { display: none }</style>
    <img src="/files/pixel.gif?page=ice-age" alt="">
